== Notes ==
* The passive item {{i|Daddy Longlegs}} is a familiar form of this boss, stomping enemies to assist Isaac. The familiar will even attack the Daddy Long Legs.
* On rooms where Daddy Long Legs is treated as a degraded Boss, they can be used to blow open doors.
* {{dlc|nr}} Like {{e|Mom}}'s stomp, his stomp deals explosive damage.

== Trivia ==
* Daddy Long Legs was added in the ''Wrath of the Lamb'' DLC for the original ''The Binding of Isaac''.
** In the original game, Daddy Long Legs could be encountered in {{s|Necropolis}}.
* Daddy Long Legs's appendages consist of 2 hands and 2 legs; he will use each of them once in his stomping attacks.
** Only 3 appendages visually appear to be connected to his head despite him having 4.
* Daddy Long Legs is a colloquialism for various types of arachnids including [[wikipedia:Opiliones|Opiliones]] and [[wikipedia:Pholcidae|Pholcidae]].
* {{e|Triachnid}} is his alternative version.
* His limbs are also used in the {{i|Daddy Longlegs}} item.

== Bugs ==
{{bug|dlc=ana+|During the mass-stomp attack, the player will take damage before the animation even begins, making it impossible to dodge.}}
{{bug|During the mass-stomp attack, if the player deals damage to one of the legs that would normally kill a full health Daddy Long Legs, it will cause the leg to die as a separate Daddy Long Legs. This will not damage the boss at all.}}
{{bug|If you [[petrification|freeze]] one of Daddy Long Legs's legs, then kill Daddy Long Legs while a Spider is still alive, then kill the Spider, the boss fight music won't stop. This is fixed if Isaac leaves the room and then re-enters again.}}

